decisions.choice:
In the end-to-end formatting test the producer's src/lib.rs differs in content from the base, not only in layout: the base commits `pub fn one() -> u32 {
    1
}
`; the producer writes that function plus a new mis-formatted `pub fn two( )->u32{2}`. The asserted formatted text is `pub fn one() -> u32 {
    1
}

pub fn two() -> u32 {
    2
}
`.

steps:
In run/tests.rs add the end-to-end formatting test `a_job_whose_only_defect_is_rustfmt_layout_passes_a_cargo_fmt_check_and_the_candidate_holds_the_formatted_file`: `commit_file` Cargo.toml, rust-toolchain.toml and a base src/lib.rs `pub fn one() -> u32 {
    1
}
`; a script wrapper whose producer turn edits README.md and writes src/lib.rs with `one` plus a mis-formatted new `pub fn two( )->u32{2}`; `athena_with(.., FMT_CHECK, ..)`; `go`; assert Landed, candidate changes are exactly README.md and src/lib.rs, `show_file` equals the formatted text (which differs from the base and the producer text), and a `format` UI line exists.

demonstrations.method:
The same end-to-end formatted-path test, after `go`: load `Records::load(&athena.git, &athena.head())`, take `jobs[id].candidate`, assert `candidate.changes` lists README.md and src/lib.rs and nothing else. The producer's src/lib.rs is the base function plus a new mis-formatted `pub fn two( )->u32{2}`, so the formatted file still differs from the base. Assert `athena.git.show_file(candidate_commit, "src/lib.rs")` equals `pub fn one() -> u32 {
    1
}

pub fn two() -> u32 {
    2
}
` and differs from the producer's text. Assert the `Lines` capture holds a line starting `format`. The pure test `paths_added_by_format_names_only_new_paths` checks the added-paths helper. If `cargo fmt` writes a Cargo.lock the base commits one.
